```javascript
// Node.js Cloud Function sketch (checkSpend.js)
const {BigQuery} = require('@google-cloud/bigquery');
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
const bq = new BigQuery();
exports.checkSpend = async (req, res) => {
  // extract date, project/service from req; run SQL to compute baseline and yesterday spend
  // if anomaly, post to Slack and write alert to BigQuery with insertId
  res.status(200).send('ok');
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle missing days in the baseline?
- How would you test this in a sandbox without real billing data?

